---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CommandSnippet from '../components/CommandSnippet.astro';
import { INSTALL_COMMAND, LAUNCH_COMMAND, PLATFORMS } from '../lib/platforms';

const mac = PLATFORMS[2];
const apps = [
  ['lucide:boxes', 'Apps and tools', 'Browse 82 Homebrew apps, terminal tools and fonts across focused categories. Magus marks what is already installed and keeps one review basket.'],
  ['lucide:wand-sparkles', 'Portable app setups', 'Apply or export curated setups for Ghostty, Zed and Firefox, extend Zsh with modern tools, and follow a guided Raycast checklist.'],
  ['lucide:rotate-ccw', 'Changes you can undo', 'Finder preferences and managed configuration files keep their original values. Restore refuses to overwrite settings you edited later.'],
];
---

<Base title="Mac — Magus alpha" description="Install the Magus Mac alpha, choose Homebrew apps and reversible settings, and apply portable setups for Ghostty, Zed, Firefox, Zsh and Raycast.">
  <div class="site-frame inner-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <a class="breadcrumb" href="/start">Platforms <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> {mac.name}</a>
      <span class="status-badge live">{mac.status}</span>
      <h1>A fresh start.<br /><span class="gradient-text">For your Mac.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">Choose your essentials, review every change, and keep the setup portable. The Mac alpha installs a native binary for Apple silicon and Intel Macs.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="site-section mac-feature-grid" aria-label="Mac alpha features">
      {apps.map(([icon, title, copy]) => (
        <article>
          <span class="benefit-icon"><Icon name={icon} aria-hidden="true" /></span>
          <h2>{title}</h2>
          <p>{copy}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </section>

    <div class="install-layout">
      <div class="install-steps">
        <section class="install-step"><span class="step-index">01</span><div>
          <h2>Install Magus.</h2>
          <p>Paste this into Terminal. It downloads the right native binary, verifies its checksum, and installs it into <code>~/.local/bin</code>.</p>
          <CommandSnippet command={INSTALL_COMMAND} label="Install command" />
          <p class="step-note">The installer adds Magus only. It does not install apps or change settings.</p>
        </div></section>
        <section class="install-step"><span class="step-index">02</span><div>
          <h2>Open the menu.</h2>
          <p>Open a new Terminal window, then launch Magus. It inspects this Mac before showing your basket.</p>
          <CommandSnippet command={LAUNCH_COMMAND} label="Launch Magus" />
          <p>Browse apps, tools, fonts, Mac settings, presets, updates, terminal choices and app setups. Nothing changes until you review and apply the basket.</p>
        </div></section>
        <section class="install-step"><span class="step-index">03</span><div>
          <h2>Make the apps yours.</h2>
          <p><strong>App setups</strong> includes three managed files—Ghostty, Zed and Firefox—plus modern command choices and a Raycast guide with selected extension links.</p>
          <p>Existing files are backed up before replacement. You can export each setup instead when you would rather merge it yourself.</p>
        </div></section>
        <section class="install-step"><span class="step-index">04</span><div>
          <h2>Return safely.</h2>
          <p>Use <code>./magus doctor</code> to inspect the saved setup without changing it, <code>./magus reconcile</code> to reapply it, and <code>./magus restore</code> to restore recorded settings.</p>
        </div></section>
      </div>

      <aside class="device-notes" aria-label="Mac alpha notes">
        <div class="device-note"><Icon name="simple-icons:apple" aria-hidden="true" /><h2>Mac alpha</h2><span class="status-badge live">Apple silicon &amp; Intel</span><p>The menu, Homebrew catalogue, update review and reversible preferences are implemented and covered by automated macOS checks.</p></div>
        <div class="device-note"><h2>App setups</h2><p>Ghostty, Zed, Firefox, modern commands and Raycast were ported from the earlier Machinist/Athanor work and adapted to Magus's review flow.</p></div>
        <div class="device-note"><h2>Alpha boundaries</h2><p>Live Zed and Firefox behaviour still needs wider testing. Firefox copies values from <code>user.js</code>, so restoring that file does not reset preferences it already loaded.</p><a href="https://github.com/gnosticgeek/magus.sh/blob/main/magus/APP_SETUPS.md">Read the setup notes ↗</a></div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <section class="troubleshooting site-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU APPLY</p><h2>Clear boundaries for an alpha.</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details><summary>Will Magus replace my existing configuration?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Only after you select a setup and approve it in Review &amp; apply. Managed files are backed up, symlinked paths are refused, and later edits are left untouched. Export a preset when you want to merge individual values.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What does the Raycast setup change?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Nothing automatically. Magus provides a checklist for Spotlight, clipboard history, snippets, Hyper Key, root search and Auto Quit, plus links to six useful extensions. Raycast remains in control of its own data.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I update apps installed outside Magus?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Yes. Update all inspects eligible Homebrew packages from the whole machine, shows the versions it found, and asks for a separate review before starting.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Where are my choices saved?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>The declarative selection lives in <code>~/.config/magus/manifest.toml</code>. Backups and run outcomes stay in Magus's local state directory.</p></details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
